%# ==== 5 ====
\section{Scoring method}
\BLOCK{if finding_scoring == 'authoritative_retained_publication'}
Finding severity, lifecycle score, and priority are copied verbatim from the retained verified finding.
No CVSS vector, presentation priority, process-assurance score, or coverage-derived rating is calculated.
The overall rating preserves the most severe non-refuted authoritative finding severity.
\BLOCK{else}
\subsection{Finding priority}
Lane 12 computes the CVSS 4.0 score $S_f$ from the vector. Priority adjusts it by how strong the
evidence is, whether it survived verification, whether the code is reachable, and exploitation signals:
\[ P_f = \min\!\big(10,\; S_f \cdot e_f \cdot v_f \cdot r_f \cdot t_f\big), \qquad t_f = 1 + \beta_{\mathrm{KEV}}\,\mathbf{1}[\mathrm{KEV}] + \beta_{\mathrm{EPSS}}\,\mathrm{EPSS}_f \]
\begin{center}\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{\qquad}ll@{\qquad}ll@{}}
\toprule
\multicolumn{2}{@{}l}{\eyebrow{Evidence $e$}} & \multicolumn{2}{l}{\eyebrow{Verification $v$}} & \multicolumn{2}{l@{}}{\eyebrow{Reachability $r$}}\\
\midrule
%% set E = scoring.evidence_weight|dictsort_insertion
%% set V = scoring.verification_weight|dictsort_insertion
%% set R = scoring.reachability_weight|dictsort_insertion
%% for i in range([E|length, V|length, R|length]|max)
\BLOCK{if i < E|length}\VAR{E[i][0]|tex} & \VAR{E[i][1]}\BLOCK{else} & \BLOCK{endif} & \BLOCK{if i < V|length}\VAR{V[i][0]|tex} & \VAR{V[i][1]}\BLOCK{else} & \BLOCK{endif} & \BLOCK{if i < R|length}\VAR{R[i][0]|tex} & \VAR{R[i][1]}\BLOCK{else} & \BLOCK{endif}\\
%% endfor
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
$\beta_{\mathrm{KEV}} = \VAR{scoring.kev_bonus}$, $\beta_{\mathrm{EPSS}} = \VAR{scoring.epss_bonus}$. Severity bands follow CVSS 4.0 qualitative ratings applied to $P_f$.

\subsection{Process assurance}
\[ c_i = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{OK}\\ \text{coverage}_i & \text{OK\_WITH\_GAPS}\\ 0 & \text{BLOCKED, FAILED, NOT\_BUILT}\\ \varnothing & \text{SKIPPED\_NA (with probe receipt)} \end{cases}
\qquad A_k = \frac{1}{|K_k|}\sum_{i\in K_k} c_i \cdot \kappa_k \]
$\kappa_k$ is the native tier cap (A $=\VAR{scoring.tier_cap.A}$, B $=\VAR{scoring.tier_cap.B}$, C $=\VAR{scoring.tier_cap.C}$), applied only to the native family.

\subsection{Overall rating}
\[ \text{rating} = \operatorname{band}\Big(\max_{f\,\notin\,\text{refuted}} P_f\Big), \qquad \text{rating} \in \{\text{None},\text{Low}\} \wedge A < \VAR{scoring.assurance_floor_for_clean} \;\Rightarrow\; \text{Indeterminate} \]
A low score is only reported as low when enough of the process ran to support it.
\BLOCK{endif}

